{
  "format": "stasium.world_monsters",
  "format_version": 1,
  "status": "proposed",
  "notes": [
    "Open-world monster packs and rare world bosses (package Z1). Numbers are Proposed; tests/sim_world_mobs.gd checks them.",
    "Rule (Mauro, 12 Oct 2026): open-world monsters are never dungeon monsters. No world id, name, art id or sheet may match any monster, escort or boss in data/world/dungeon_monsters.json or its art under art/pc/dungeons/. run_world_mobs_tests.gd fails on a match.",
    "Base values are at each row's level_min; every level above adds hp_per_level of the base HP and damage_per_level of the base damage (the dungeon rule).",
    "Pack levels follow the chunk's depth (level_zones.json depth) inside the zone band: the shallowest pack chunk sits at the band floor, the deepest at its top; a pack spans 3 levels.",
    "Pack sizes 2-10 (Mauro, Wakfu style): size_weights are per depth; big packs only deeper in the zone.",
    "Rewards: the spec 4.8 world-fight XP and the world coins are for a pack of base_pack monsters; a pack of n gets (n / base_pack) ^ size_exponent of that. Gear chance x (1 + drop_per_extra x (n - 1)).",
    "Bosses spawn only while their condition holds: one roll per in-condition minute in the zone, then a cooldown. They leave when the condition ends or after timeout_s.",
    "Weather ids are crosshaven_weather.gd's (clear, light_cloud, light_rain, wind). fog, storm and snow are accepted but have no weather look yet, so a boss that needs them never spawns until one exists.",
    "The orchard and mill chunks are thin strips (36x4, 36x6) between the town and the fields: they hold two small packs each (max_size), a 1-cell edge margin on their short side, and the fight board there is the strip itself. The orchard rows and the windmill stand in the fields chunk, so the three bosses spawn there."
  ],
